      "problem": "${log}_{3}⁡(\\frac{1}{81})=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite $\\frac{1}{81}$ as a power of $3$ (the base of the logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{81}=\\frac{1}{{3}^{4}}={3}^{-4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n{log}_{3}⁡(\\frac{1}{81})={log}_{3}⁡({3}^{-4})\n$$\n\nThe logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n{log}_{b}⁡({b}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $b=3$ and $x=-4.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n{log}_{3}⁡({3}^{-4})=-4\n$$",
